# Level 6 → Level 7

## Concept
This one drops you in with almost no lead - just three facts about 
a file (owner, group, and exact size) and no idea where on the server 
it actually lives. It's less about a specific command and more about 
knowing how to search a whole filesystem by properties instead of 
just looking around folder by folder.

## Commands used
find / -user bandit7 -group bandit6 -size 33c 
cat /path/it/found

## Why it works
find / starts the search from the very top of the filesystem instead 
of just the current folder. Stacking -user, -group, and -size together 
means only a file matching all three conditions gets returned, which 
narrows an entire server down to basically a few files.
